<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Home-screen widget (V1 Req 36), widget spec §7 Step 7.

   The two declared sizes bracket what tested launchers actually report for a 2×1 and a 4×2 cell;
   `WidgetContent` branches on height alone, so any size in between still picks the right variant.

   updatePeriodMillis=1800000 (the platform minimum — smaller values are clamped): a revision of
   the original 0. The app still drives every refresh itself (snapshot writes, resize callback),
   but the platform's periodic update is the backstop the original comment missed — when the app
   process is dead or freezer-SIGSTOPped no app-side writer can run, and this broadcast is what
   cold-starts/thaws it (only a force-stopped app is unreachable, which no widget mechanism can
   fix). Found by the 2026-10-14 widget-staleness investigation. Glance's receiver handles
   ACTION_APPWIDGET_UPDATE through the standard GlanceAppWidgetReceiver path.

   previewImage is a capture of the real 4×2 render (drawable-nodpi/widget_preview.png), not a
   mock-up: it is what the widget actually looks like in Desert Dawn, so the launcher picker cannot
   promise a design the widget doesn't draw. Re-capture from the device if the layout changes.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:description="@string/widget_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:minHeight="40dp"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/widget_preview"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:targetCellWidth="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    tools:targetApi="31" />
